{"id": "EUVD-2026-103668", "enisaUuid": "2492c40a-f492-326c-ac78-a785fef5e216", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/nouveau/clk: fix list cursor use after loop in nvkm_clk_ustate_update\n\nIf list_for_each_entry() exits without hitting a break then \"pstate\" is\nnot a valid pstate pointer.  Introduce a \"found\" variable instead.\n\nThe check is reachable from userspace: nvkm_clk_ustate_update() takes the\npstate id straight from the 'pstate' debugfs file, so requesting an id\nthat is not in clk->states - or any id at all when the perf tables are\nbroken and the list is empty - makes the pstate->pstate != req test\ndereference the list head cast to a struct nvkm_pstate, which is an\nout-of-bounds read.\n\n[Francesco: rebased on drm-misc-next, expanded the commit message]", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:51", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/db5dd9f47b4df1be322f498d846e9a82940a7390", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d550924961f61a491dd95359c63494fa8a23d9f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/492e9cfa12f35f7946ea1b78a19f1f9337d62248", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a867abcfa85ab487066c3d3008a1ba905da04113", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5315c7bacfe274ddfe649d9556e9a341ffa812da", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0d096a7f7d79207490858dde731b16da5337e90c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/391517da7fd54ae40e4a7fe1cc696217343b0061", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aff09d9e37e02dc60bde79035ac15b136d602259"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98623", "GHSA-5c9q-m24x-7r34"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00fa9832-edc5-3b47-b85e-150409ec8951", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7c856522069755ab9d163a24ac332cd3cb35fe30 <0d096a7f7d79207490858dde731b16da5337e90c"}, {"id": "22fd6b24-2d48-3733-8250-f1650140a455", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_versi